text
```
` A strange signal arrives in the middle of the night.
%BLACK
/Violet
$ Hello? Is anyone there?
/Radio
$ ...ksssshhh...
/Violet
$ Great. Either the radio is broken, or my house is haunted.
_
/Violet
$ I should probably turn it off.
?Turn off the radio|OFF&Listen closer|LISTEN

@OFF
%BLACK
/Violet
$ I reach over and twist the dial until the static disappears.
$ For a moment, the room is completely silent.
$ Then something knocks on my bedroom door.
_
/Violet
$ ...I live alone.
?Open the door|DOOR&Hide in the closet|CLOSET

@DOOR
%VIOLET1
/Violet
$ I slowly reach for the handle.
$ The door swings open by itself.
$ There's nobody in the hallway, but a small piece of paper rests on the floor.
_
/Violet
$ It has my name written on it.
$ Underneath, in handwriting that looks exactly like mine, are the words:
$ "You shouldn't have turned it off."
?Pick up the paper|PAPER&Leave it alone|IGNORE

@PAPER
%STARS
/Violet
$ I pick up the paper.
$ The moment my fingers touch it, every light in the house goes out.
$ Through the window, I see the night sky filled with stars.
$ Too many stars.
$ They seem to be moving, slowly arranging themselves into letters.
_
/Violet
$ No. No, no, no.
$ The stars spell out a single word.
$ LISTEN.
%RADIO
$ From somewhere behind me, the radio switches itself back on.
$ ...ksssshhh...
/Radio
$ Violet.
_
/Violet
$ It knows my name.
?Answer the voice|ANSWER&Run outside|RUN

@ANSWER
%BLACK
/Violet
$ Who are you?
/Radio
$ I am the part of you that stayed behind.
_
/Violet
$ What does that even mean?
/Radio
$ You were never supposed to wake up.
$ You were supposed to forget.
$ But you heard the signal, and now the door is open.
$ Look outside.
%STARS
/Violet
$ The stars are gone.
$ In their place is a vast, dark emptiness, stretching across the entire sky.
$ Something enormous moves beyond the glass.
$ I can hear it breathing.
_
/Violet
$ What happens now?
/Radio
$ Now you choose which side of the door you want to be on.
?Ask what is outside|OUTSIDE&Destroy the radio|DESTROY

@OUTSIDE
%VIOLET1
/Violet
$ I step toward the window.
$ The thing outside stops moving.
$ A pale hand presses against the glass.
$ Then another.
$ Then dozens more.
$ They all look like my hands.
_
/Violet
$ I understand now.
$ The room, the radio, the stars. None of it is real.
$ I'm not in my house.
$ I'm inside something that's trying to remember what a house looks like.
%BLACK
/Radio
$ And it remembers you.
_
/Violet
$ I back away from the window, but the walls begin to fold inward.
$ The radio emits one final burst of static.
$ Then everything goes dark.
!
@DESTROY
%RADIO
/Violet
$ I grab the radio and slam it against the floor.
$ Plastic cracks. Metal scatters across the carpet.
$ The static cuts off.
$ For three seconds, nothing happens.
_
/Violet
$ Then every broken piece begins to whisper.
%BLACK
/Radio
$ You can break the receiver.
$ You cannot break the signal.
$ You can silence the voice.
$ You cannot silence the thing listening through it.
$ And you cannot destroy a door by smashing the key.
_
/Violet
$ The floor opens beneath me.
$ I fall through darkness, past fragments of rooms I recognize.
$ My childhood bedroom.
$ The school I used to attend.
$ A street I have never visited, beneath a sky full of violet stars.
%STARS
/Violet
$ I land on cold ground.
$ Somewhere in the distance, a radio begins to play.
$ I don't know how long I walk toward it.
$ I only know that, eventually, I hear my own voice coming through the speakers.
/Radio
$ Hello? Is anyone there?
!
@LISTEN
%RADIO
/Violet
$ I turn the dial a little farther.
$ Beneath the static, there's a faint melody.
$ I recognize it, though I can't remember where I've heard it before.
$ Then a voice begins speaking in a language I don't understand.
$ Somehow, I understand every word.
/Radio
$ The stars are not stars.
$ The darkness is not empty.
$ And you are not where you think you are.
_
/Violet
$ I pull the radio closer.
$ The voice sounds frightened.
$ It sounds like me.
?Ask who is speaking|VOICE&Change the frequency|FREQUENCY

@VOICE
%VIOLET1
/Violet
$ Who is this?
/Radio
$ You.
$ From tomorrow.
_
/Violet
$ That's impossible.
/Radio
$ I said the same thing.
$ Listen carefully. At midnight, someone will knock on your door.
$ Do not open it.
$ No matter what it says, do not open it.
$ Especially if it sounds like me.
%BLACK
/Violet
$ The radio clicks off.
$ I stare at the clock.
$ 11:59 PM.
$ A knock comes from the front door.
_
/Violet
$ Then another.
$ Then a familiar voice calls from the other side.
/Radio
$ Violet? It's me. Please let me in.
?Open the door|DOOR&Stay silent|CLOSET

@FREQUENCY
%BLACK
/Violet
$ I spin the dial as quickly as I can.
$ The melody disappears.
$ Voices blur into static, then into a low, rhythmic pulse.
$ Thump.
$ Thump.
$ Thump.
_
/Violet
$ It's a heartbeat.
$ I press my ear against the speaker.
$ The heartbeat stops.
$ My own heart stops with it.
%STARS
/Violet
$ For one impossible moment, I see myself floating among the stars.
$ I see a thousand versions of my house, each with a radio glowing in its window.
$ In every house, someone is listening.
$ In every house, someone is about to open a door.
$ Then I hear a voice behind me.
/Radio
$ Finally. I've found you.
?Turn around|TURN&Keep listening|VOICE

@TURN
%VIOLET1
/Violet
$ I turn around.
$ Standing in the corner is a person wearing my face.
$ They look exhausted.
$ Their clothes are torn, their hands are trembling, and their eyes reflect a sky full of stars.
_
/Violet
$ Who are you?
/Radio
$ I'm the version of you who made the wrong choice.
$ And I've come to make sure you don't repeat it.
$ There's only one way out.
$ You have to stop the story before it reaches the end.
%BLACK
/Violet
$ How?
/Radio
$ Find the first sound.
$ Find the first word.
$ Find the moment you decided to listen.
$ Then do what I couldn't.
?Return to the beginning|LISTEN&Refuse to help|REFUSE

@REFUSE
%BLACK
/Violet
$ I shake my head.
$ I'm tired of voices, riddles, and impossible choices.
$ I want my house back.
$ I want the radio gone.
$ I want to sleep.
_
/Violet
$ So I close my eyes.
$ When I open them, morning sunlight spills across my bedroom.
$ The radio is gone.
$ The door is closed.
$ Everything seems normal.
%STARS
/Violet
$ I make coffee. I get dressed. I go about my day.
$ And for a while, I convince myself that it was all a dream.
$ Until that evening, when I find a small piece of paper on my kitchen table.
$ It has my name written on it.
$ Underneath are the words:
$ "Tomorrow, try listening."
!
@CLOSET
%BLACK
/Violet
$ I run into the closet and pull the door shut.
$ I crouch between winter coats and boxes of old belongings.
$ Outside, footsteps cross the room.
$ They stop directly in front of the closet.
_
/Violet
$ A hand touches the other side of the door.
$ Then a voice whispers.
/Radio
$ Violet, I know you're in there.
$ I know because I'm in here too.
%VIOLET1
/Violet
$ The closet door slowly swings open.
$ There's no hallway beyond it.
$ No bedroom.
$ No house.
$ Only another closet, with another frightened version of me hiding inside.
$ She looks up at me.
$ She opens her mouth to speak.
$ And I hear my own voice coming from the radio behind her.
!
```
